transip-rest (0.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add a PATCH-based `update_dns_entry()` to the client and a matching
    `transip-dns update` CLI subcommand, so changing an existing record
    (e.g. an MX target) no longer needs a separate delete-then-add.
    TransIP's PATCH /domains/{domain}/dns identifies the entry to change
    by name+expire+type (confirmed verbatim from
    https://api.transip.nl/rest/docs.html, "Update single DNS entry") -
    only `content` is the new value; this does not attempt to change a
    record's ttl or type itself, which the API docs do not document a
    way to do via PATCH.
  * Add `--credentials-ini FILE` to the CLI as an alternative to passing
    `--username`/`--key-file` on every call - reads the same
    `dns_transip_username`/`dns_transip_key_file` keys the
    certbot-dns-transip plugin's own credentials file already uses, so
    one credentials file serves both tools. Mutually exclusive with
    `--username`/`--key-file`; exactly one form is required.
  * 9 new tests (1 for update_dns_entry, 8 for the new CLI credential
    resolution and update-subcommand parsing) - 34 total, all passing.

